{
  "_comment": [
    "Synthetic gen3 FireRed scenario (plan 2.7 for gen3; decision 6 says a recording needs Scott):",
    "a new game, the starter, a route change, one wild battle, the Brock fight with a party switch,",
    "a level up with a new move, a badge, a blackout and a reset. FireRed rather than Emerald because a",
    "fresh profile's game is 'FireRed and LeafGreen' in the legacy app and the Emerald mapper carries no",
    "meta.gameName to correct it (known-legacy-bugs.md #12); the starter is the legacy default, Rayquaza,",
    "so the party leader is Rayquaza too (synthetic: values are chosen, not played).",
    "It is built to touch the hooks in gen3's mounted() on the non-legacy (sStpCallback) state path:",
    "  pointers.sStpCallback2 CB2_MainMenu -> CB2_NewGameScene   new run (attempt++, ROM starter writes)",
    "  overworld.mapName change                  OBS 'Map Change - <map>' marker",
    "  patch.sStpTextBoxOpen 1 / 0               'Text Box - true' / 'Text Box - false' markers",
    "  sStpCallback2 CB2_InitBattle / BattleMainCB2 / CB2_Overworld",
    "                                            To Battle, 'IN - <trainer>' / 'OUT - <trainer>' markers",
    "  battle.turnInfo.battleDialogue 6          Battle (FRLG's dialogue is a bare int; 6 is player control)",
    "  battle.turnInfo.battleOutcome 1 + battle.type.trainer",
    "                                            From Battle, Full/Deprecated/Simple split CSVs, 'LABEL - VICTORY'",
    "  battle.trainer.party_position change      'Next Pokemon' marker",
    "  player.team.0.level / move2 change        level-up handling, 'New Move - <name>' marker",
    "  player.badges.badge1 true                 badge boosts",
    "  sStpCallback2 CB2_WhiteOut                blackout (blackout_counter++, 'BLACKOUT')",
    "  sStpCallback2 CB2_InitCopyrightScreenAfterBootup, then both callbacks null",
    "                                            reset (playerResets++, Base Stats, 'RESET')",
    "The Pewter part starts at 62 s so the Brock split lands after the timer's first minute, as gen4's",
    "does. Referenced properties carry the glossary value the recorder would have written. Every path is",
    "checked against the mapper XML at build time. Values are plausible, not a real run: this fixture",
    "proves determinism and no-change-under-refactor, never correctness (see make-fixture.ts)."
  ],
